v 3
d 'RTMTOOLS': Stata tools for the design and weighting of real-time monitoring phone surveys
d
d rtmtools gives task teams Stata commands with dialog boxes (User > RTM tools) for
d the weights of a phone panel round (base weights, nonresponse and attrition
d adjustment, trimming, calibration to population totals, weighting report), for
d design-based estimates with design effects and coefficients of variation, and for
d sample sizes, allocation across strata and probability draws from a frame.
d Statistical steps run through svycal, svyset and svy, survwgt and ipfraking;
d the ReGenesees calibration features run through R in the background, optional.
d Method defaults cite the HFPS sampling guidelines (Himelein et al. 2020), the
d Listening to Tajikistan methods report, Ambel et al. 2021 and UN 2008.
d
d KW: survey weights
d KW: calibration
d KW: nonresponse adjustment
d KW: phone survey
d KW: real-time monitoring
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 (svycal: Stata 18); survwgt, ipfraking, gsample and moremata from SSC for the corresponding steps
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261024
d
d Author: Real-Time Monitoring Survey Handbook task team, World Bank
d
